From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:28:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] generate_qmap: add the camera and programmable keys

KEY_CAMERA, KEY_CAMERA_FOCUS, KEY_MACRO and KEY_PROG1 are in neither Qt's
default table nor this one, so the evdev handler drops them before any Qt key
event exists and the shell cannot act on them however it is configured.

Phones have them. A shutter key reports KEY_CAMERA_FOCUS on a half press and
KEY_CAMERA on a full press. The FuriLabs FLX1s has an assistant button on its
volume keypad that its kernel maps to KEY_MACRO (112), and the same phone's
camera privacy switch reports its position as KEY_CAMERA. That last one is
why these get their keycodes' own meanings here and nothing more, as the
toolbelt keys did: whether KEY_CAMERA opens the camera is a per-device
decision for the shell, and on that phone the answer is no.

Key_Launch0 already belongs to KEY_EMOJI_PICKER, so KEY_PROG1 and KEY_MACRO
take Key_Launch1 and Key_Launch2 and stay distinguishable from it and from
each other.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
+++ b/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
@@ -36,7 +36,17 @@
     // printed on the key faces rather than acting as a modifier; see the
     // bbqX0kbd patches. Key_Launch0 carries no meaning of its own, which
     // leaves what the key does to the layer that knows the keyboard.
-    { 585, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch0,  0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }  // KEY_EMOJI_PICKER
+    { 585, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch0,  0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_EMOJI_PICKER
+
+    // Camera and programmable keys. As above, each keycode gets its own Qt
+    // key and what the key does is the shell's per-device decision: on one
+    // phone KEY_CAMERA is a shutter key, on another a privacy switch.
+    // Key_Launch0 is taken by the emoji picker, so the programmable keys
+    // start at Key_Launch1.
+    { 112, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch2,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_MACRO
+    { 148, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch1,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_PROG1
+    { 212, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Camera,      0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_CAMERA
+    { 528, 0xffff, Qt::Key_CameraFocus, 0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }  // KEY_CAMERA_FOCUS
 };
 
 #endif // WEBOS_KEYMAP_P_H
